{
  "comment": [
    "Pinned identities of the stock Xiaomi Fastboot ROM images that the dual",
    "layout writes to the Android slot.  These are checksums of a published",
    "vendor package, not secrets: they exist so that the installer refuses a",
    "ROM directory that is not the pinned release. Device validation is",
    "recorded separately. The ROM is an upstream input, not redistributed",
    "here.  'partition' is always the _a slot name (or the non-slotted super);",
    "the installer never writes _b apart from boot_b with the project image.",
    "boot.img is the exception to flashing: in the dual layout both systems",
    "boot from slot A, so boot_a receives the project image and boot.img (or",
    "the --android-boot override) is stored on the Ubuntu root, from where",
    "liuqin-switch writes it to the 'partition' named here.",
    "'sparse' marks an Android sparse image, whose bytes cannot be compared",
    "against the partition content, so it is always flashed when requested."
  ],
